  "_": "The number rules (spec/device-api.md, *Numbers*) as a table of cases, which the reference backend and the app are both tested against, so a backend of your own can read every number the same way. A context is the SIM's home. A case names its context and what was typed or delivered (`in`); `stored` is how it is kept — exactly that, less grouping, never completed (`\"\"` when nothing in it is a number); `kind` and `number` are what reading it finds (international, service, gateway, unresolved; null for no digits); `pretty` is how the app shows it — the stored digits grouped, nothing added or removed; `place`/`carrier`, where given, are what the reference backend's lookup returns for a Chinese reader: informative, and a backend's own place data may differ. All numbers here are examples chosen for their format; do not call or text them.",
